[Gemini translation of the Kannada text, not printed in the volume -- verify]
26. four grants, authorities, transformations, and transactions;
27. you may take and enjoy them properly with your sons, grandsons, and through successive generations as long as the moon and sun endure;
28-31. to Rāvalsha Prāṇāchāri, the son of Veṅkaṭabhaṭṭa, who was the grandson of Ānantabhaṭṭa, belonging to the... gotra, [Āpastamba?] sūtra, and Yajur-śākhā... the leaders of... and the leaders having caused to be written...
32-36. Bhūdāna-śāsana. Verse: "Better than making a gift is protection; there is no merit higher than protection..." "Whosoever takes back land given by himself or by another, he is born as a worm in dung for sixty thousand years..." (In the large plate) Śrī-Rāvanīśvara.
